WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.430
- [Instructor] We're asked
what is the value of the point

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.670
graphed on the number line
and this is the point right

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.317
over here, so pause this video
and see if you can figure

00:00:09.317 --> 00:00:11.983
that out before we figure it out together.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.350
All right so let's try to
figure it out together now.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.250
So let's see this point is
between this is going to be

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.150
this is the tenths place
this is the hundredths place

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.350
so this over here is three
hundredths and this over here

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.240
is four hundredths.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:36.050
So our point is between three
hundredths and four hundredths

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.980
and the space between three
hundredths and four hundredths

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.910
is divided into ten equal spaces.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:47.910
So if this whole thing is
a hundredth, so this whole

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.610
thing is equal to 0.01 the
difference between that,

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.790
that's a hundredth so then
each tenth of that is going

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.268
to be a thousandth.

00:00:58.268 --> 00:01:01.030
So let me, I don't want to
make this too messy so this

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:04.890
right over here will be
one tenth of a hundredth

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.890
which is going to be a thousandth,
so it's going to be 0.001

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.088
we have a one in the thousandths place.

00:01:13.088 --> 00:01:16.205
So one way to think about it,
this number is going to be

00:01:16.205 --> 00:01:21.205
0.03 so we have our three
hundredths but then let's see

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.890
how many thousandths we have
to add to it to get to this

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.210
value right over here.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.370
We have to add one
thousandth, two thousandths,

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:34.921
three thousandths, four
thousandths, five thousandths,

00:01:34.921 --> 00:01:39.921
six thousandths, seven
thousandths, and eight thousandths.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:44.267
So we're starting at three
hundredths and then we are adding

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:49.267
eight thousandths so you add
0.008 to get to this value.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.990
So if you were to add these
two together you're going

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.120
to have three hundredths
and then the next place over

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.390
is the thousandths place
and we have eight of them.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:05.390
So this point right over
here is 0.038 or you could do

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:10.610
this as 38 thousandths
because three hundredths is 30

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.040
thousandths, so any way you
want to view it, this is

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.653
the value of the point graphed
on the number line 0.038.

